{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd && source .venv/bin/activate && python .codex/skills/literature-review/scripts/verify_citations.py literature_review.md && test -s .resource_finder_complete && echo completion_marker=ok && sed -n '/NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START:resource_finder/,/NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_END:resource_finder/p' STATE.md && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"/workspaces/is-there-a-sounds-like-ai-direction-cc6e-codex-gpt-5-6-sol\nCitation Analysis: literature_review.md\n==================================================\n\nTotal citations found: 13\n\nBy type:\n  arxiv: 11\n  doi: 1\n  inline: 1\n\ncompletion_marker=ok\n<!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START:resource_finder -->\nPhase `resource_finder` completed 2026-10-03. Gathered and validated 12 PDFs, four required datasets, and six official repositories; wrote `literature_review.md`, `resources.md`, `planning.md`, and per-directory READMEs. Core specified papers were split into 43 three-page chunks and fully reviewed; searchable text is in `artifacts/fulltexts/`.\n\nKey finding: human/AI text is robustly linearly decodable, but existing MGT probe papers do not causally steer free generation. The closest causal work changes self-authorship judgments, while SAE and Assistant Axis results show strong formality/verbosity/persona confounds. HAP-E is the primary paired identification dataset; MAGE and RAID are independent OOD/stress tests.\n\nDirection budget fixed in `planning.md`: (1) signed causal steering with supervised human→AI directions, (2) Assistant/style nuisance residualization, and (3) layer/model transfer with paired counterfactual validation. Rejected directions and reasons are recorded there.\n\nNext phase: implement on an open 8B instruct/base pair using HAP-E document-level splits; reuse `code/sv-detect`, `code/mgt_probes`, RepE hooks, and `code/assistant-axis`; evaluate with independent MAGE/RAID-trained detectors plus content/coherence metrics. Full RAID was not downloaded because its source is 16.7 GB; a reproducible 4,800-row coverage sample and full-download instructions are in `datasets/`. GPU execution remains unresolved and requires a compatible CUDA host/model weights.\n\nFailures/workarounds: paper-finder returned HTTP 500, so primary-source manual search was used; `uv add` hit Hatchling empty-package detection, so dependencies were installed in the fresh `.venv` via `uv pip` and recorded in `pyproject.toml`; `pdftotext` was absent, so `pypdf` extracted each chunk.\n<!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_END:resource_finder -->\n M .gitignore\n?? .claude/\n?? .codex/\n?? .gemini/\n?? .neurico/pipeline_state.json\n?? .resource_finder_complete\n?? STATE.md\n?? artifacts/\n?? code/\n?? datasets/\n?? literature_review.md\n?? logs/\n?? paper_search_results/\n?? papers/\n?? planning.md\n?? pyproject.toml\n?? resources.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"agent_message","text":"Resource-finding phase is complete and validated.\n\nKey deliverables:\n\n- [Literature review](/workspaces/is-there-a-sounds-like-ai-direction-cc6e-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/literature_review.md)\n- [Resource catalog](/workspaces/is-there-a-sounds-like-ai-direction-cc6e-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/resources.md)\n- [Ranked research directions](/workspaces/is-there-a-sounds-like-ai-direction-cc6e-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/planning.md)\n- [Phase handoff](/workspaces/is-there-a-sounds-like-ai-direction-cc6e-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/STATE.md)\n- [Completion marker](/workspaces/is-there-a-sounds-like-ai-direction-cc6e-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/.resource_finder_complete)\n\nGathered and checked:\n\n- 12 papers, including full chunk-by-chunk review of the four specified works\n- All four requested datasets\n  - HC3, HAP-E, and MAGE complete\n  - RAID represented locally by a reproducible 4,800-row coverage sample; full source is 16.7 GB\n- 6 official code repositories, syntax-validated\n- Fresh project `.venv` and documented dependencies\n\nThe main research gap is clear: existing work demonstrates robust linear readout of machine-generated text, but does not test whether that direction causally changes free-generation style. The top experiment therefore combines signed activation steering with independent detection and explicit Assistant-axis/style-confound controls."}}
